{"name":"Tempo Teal","hex":"#018c94","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tempo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A frequency or rate.","A move which is part of one's own plan or strategy and forces, e.g. by means of a check or attacking a piece, the opponent to make a move which is not bad but of no use (the player gains a tempo, the opponent loses a tempo), or equivalently a player achieves the same result in fewer moves by one approach rather than another."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A temporary carport."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tempo"},{"term":"teal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small freshwater ducks of the genus Anas that are brightly coloured and have short necks.","A dark, somewhat bluish-green colour; a dark cyan."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a bluish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tempo","blocks":[{"text":"In musical terminology, tempo, measured in beats per minute, is the speed or pace of a given composition, and is often also an indication of the composition's character or atmosphere. In classical music, tempo is typically indicated with an instruction at the start of a piece and, if a specific metrical pace is desired, is usually measured in beats per minute. In modern classical compositions, a \"metronome mark\" in beats per minute, indicating only measured speed and not any form of expression, may supplement or replace the normal tempo marking, while in modern genres like electronic dance music, tempo will typically simply be stated in bpm."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Tempo_plots.svg/330px-Tempo_plots.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tempo"},{"title":"Teal","blocks":[{"text":"Teal is a dark cyan color. Its name comes from that of a bird, the Eurasian teal which has a similarly colored stripe on its head. The word is often used colloquially to refer to shades of cyan in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg/330px-Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg/500px-Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg/500px-Electronic-metronome%28scale%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wittner electronic metronome","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElectronic-metronome(scale).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-San_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_%2853351816983%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASan_Jose_Sharks_at_Seattle_Kraken_-_November_22%2C_2023_-_Tomas_Hertl_(53351816983)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c